				155,
				27
			],
			"Message": "Refactor scripts to improve error handling and output redirection\n\n- Updated all scripts in the Maintain and Transfer directories to use consistent output redirection style (e.g., `>/dev/null` instead of `> /dev/null`).\n- Ensured that error messages are redirected properly to avoid cluttering the console output.\n- Improved readability and maintainability of scripts by standardizing the way command outputs are handled.\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "e5c30196d030ffde870918a758586e01f919af41"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T20:04:34Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠃⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				39
			],
			"Message": "style(Land): Reflow documentation prose and finalize shell/TS formatting\n\nReflow paragraph text across Documentation/GitHub/*.md and CONTRIBUTING.md so sentences that were split across lines are combined into proper single-line paragraphs, improving readability in both rendered and source form.\n\nNormalize remaining shell script formatting in Maintain/: fix redirect operator spacing (`>/dev/null` to `> /dev/null`, `2>&1` to `2>&1` with space, `&>/dev/null` to `&> /dev/null`), align pipe continuations at end-of-line with the next command indented on the following line, and fix case-statement body indentation depth to match shfmt's `-i 4` profile across Debug/Build, Debug/Run, Dev-Mountain, Format, Integration/SmokeProfiles, List/Fork, Profile, Release, Release/Build, Repository, Save, and all Maintain/Script/ and Test/ files.\n\nRemove spurious blank lines after the `export default` block in prettier.config.js and tailwind.config.js to match Prettier's own formatting expectations.\n\nNo functional changes — purely cosmetic consistency across the Land monorepo root.",
			"SHA": "374910a8fb937e393505dd38def6de41f242e98f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T19:12:09Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				31
			],
			"Message": "style(Maintain): Normalize shell and TypeScript formatting across scripts\n\nApply shfmt formatting normalization across all Maintain shell scripts — fix case-statement indent depth, standardize redirect spacing (`>/dev/null` → `>/dev/null`), align pipe continuations to end-of-line placement, and normalize `2>&1` spacing. Add blank-line separation between import groups and after block-level declarations (async functions, interfaces) in TypeScript codegen files. Insert missing top-level blank lines in prettier.config.js and tailwind.config.js.\n\nNo functional changes — purely formatting consistency aligned with the project's shfmt and Prettier profiles.",
			"SHA": "fc363dbfb501bc585d5835e9adbe7b51f9d2ad7e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:48:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Prune unused Tauri plugin and utility crate deps\n\nRemove 23 tauri-plugin-* crates (autostart, barcode-scanner, biometric, cli, clipboard-manager, deep-link, geolocation, global-shortcut, haptics, http, nfc, notification, opener, os, persisted-scope, positioner, process, shell, single-instance, sql, store, stronghold, updater, upload, websocket, window-state), 4 Tauri tooling crates (bundler, cli, driver, macos-sign), tauri-schema-generator, and 3 utility crates (window-vibrancy, window-shadows, global-hotkey) from Cargo.toml.\n\nThese dependencies were declared but never referenced in any crate under the workspace — the editor only uses dialog, fs, localhost, and log from the plugin set. Removing them reduces workspace resolution overhead, eliminates stale pin maintenance, and makes the actual dependency surface explicit.\n\nBoth the crates.io versions and the local Dependency/Tauri/... path overrides are dropped together for each removed crate.",
			"SHA": "85e4da375ec0828818b32787dfae85b4d9bb0304"
		}
	],
